NOTICE — 05-datamixtures-and-curriculum
=======================================

WHAT THIS IS

A coursework exercise: a specification for the data mixture and curriculum of a
hypothetical India-first language model. It is a study of a decision, not a
product, not a proposal to any organisation, and not a plan anybody has committed
to. No model has been trained on this recipe.

NO AFFILIATION

This work is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or produced on behalf
of any company, government body, research institute, university, or funding
programme. Every organisation named here — dataset publishers, model developers,
benchmark owners — is named because their public work is the evidence being
examined. Naming them is citation, not association, and none of them has reviewed
or approved anything here.

WHERE THE DATASET FIGURES COME FROM

The inventory in src/mixture/inventory.py is transcribed from the Session 5 course
material, which states of its own figures that "dataset sizes are approximate and
being verified". That caveat is carried through: every row is typed `confirmed`,
`approximate` or `unstated`, and rows with no token count are recorded as having
none rather than estimated.

Two figures in the source material disagree with each other, and this exercise
follows the itemised datasets rather than the slot headline in both cases. Those
disagreements are published in SPEC.md and PROGRESS.md rather than silently
resolved. They are a reading of the material by the author of this exercise; they
may be wrong, and the arithmetic is included so anyone can check.

NO DATASET IS REDISTRIBUTED

This exercise sizes datasets; it does not host, mirror, or redistribute them. Each
dataset's own licence governs its use. Where the inventory records a licence, that
record is a reading of public material and may be out of date.

WHAT IS MEASURED AND WHAT IS NOT

- MEASURED: the reasoning-band token counts (counted with this project's own
  Session 2 vocabulary), the tokenizer fertility and [UNK] tables (measured in
  exercises 03 and 04), and every arithmetic result derived from the inventory.

- ESTIMATED, AND LABELLED SO: the supervised-token ratio for agentic trajectories,
  which converts a phrase in the course material into a range. It is deliberately
  applied at its most generous end, and the conclusion it supports does not depend
  on it — the agentic lane fails its repetition ceiling on raw, uncorrected tokens.

- NOT MEASURED, AND SAID SO: the throughput of the local machine the proxy runs
  would use. No figure is entered for it and the cost model returns an absent value
  rather than a plausible one, because a number there would decide a spending
  question on evidence nobody gathered.

- ILLUSTRATIVE, AND SAID SO: the difficulty-band examples (B0–B5) are authored to
  illustrate each level. They are not samples from any corpus, and no classifier
  assigns real documents to bands here.

THE PROXY HAS NOT BEEN RUN

SPEC.md commits to an experiment and declares its thresholds in advance. At the
time of writing, no arm has been trained and no result is reported. Any statement
about what the mixture achieves is a hypothesis, and the specification says so.
